//! store/blob bindings, and a `fetch` for granted egress hosts. Every one of
//! those is a synchronous framed RPC to the host over stdio; the host services
//! the call and re-runs the (deterministic) program with the answer appended —
//! see `engine.rs`. A lightweight TypeScript type-stripper lets the model write
//! annotated code; it erases types, it does not type-check.
//!
//! A consumer that needs additional globals (a server-function host adding
//! request/response marshalling, say) injects them through
//! [`build_program_with`]: the extra prelude runs after the standard prelude
//! and before the user code, with `ferrite`/`console`/`fetch`/`env` already
//! installed.

